     "<div dir=\"ltr\">so I am not sure what caused that. You might check your specified destination and permissions?</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">As for the error I got, it was because the destination for output files is the same as the directory holding the NewHybrid executables, and I did not expect anyone to do that. The script could not copy the file nhyb.txt on to itself. I will trap that bug in the next version. In the meantime, try specifying your working directory as the outpath with outpath=getwd().</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">The second issue of NewHybrids stopping prematurely when you generated and ran the input file manually.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">It looks like you have requested 0 sweeps for the analysis and 0 sweeps for the burning. Can you check this. Otherwise, send me your nhyb.txt file, and I will give it a try.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hope this helps.<br></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">A<br><br><pre style=\"background:white;line-height:11.25pt\"><br><br><br><br>This is because the specified<span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span><br></span></pre></div>"
